  "readmeFile": "PackageReadme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.7.0 replaces 0.6.9. It fixes data corruption on the serial link with FP3002 firmware 2.10, makes recordings, sessions, firmware updates and saved settings reliable, and makes plots faster. Workflows and settings files from 0.6.9 load unchanged.\n\nFirmware 2.10 ships with this package. Opening the Setup window offers the update; it is recommended, not required.\n\nHighlights\n- No more data gaps from the serial link. On firmware 2.9, about 1 in 43,000 commands sent to the board made it re-send old data, and 0.6.9 then lost 5 to 68 minutes of recording, depending on frame rate. Firmware 2.10 removes the cause, and 0.7.0 also discards repeated data on any firmware.\n- Correct photodiode timestamps. About once every few hours, a photodiode sample was stamped one second early.\n- Correct LED labels after a dropped camera frame.\n- The FP3002 node runs its upstream workflow once, not twice. This fixes IronPython-triggered stimulation that never fired and endless \"spontaneous disconnection\" loops.\n- Write To Persistent Registers no longer leaves the board in a bad state.\n- Firmware updates are significantly more reliable, and a board left mid-update can be rescued with a forced reflash.\n- Plots draw about 3.5 times faster with about 10 times less memory.\n- Video files no longer become unreadable past 4 GB.\n- A 0% laser amplitude now turns the laser off.\n\nOutput files\n- Saved plots are .png files, not .jpg.\n- Video and plot files now split with each CSV file.\n\nThe first time a new version runs, Windows Firewall may ask about \"Neurophotometrics Camera Server\". The request comes from the FLIR camera software inside it, and it is safe to cancel.\n\nFull release notes: https://www.mbfbioscience.com/app/uploads/2026/05/MBFpackage070updateNotes.pdf",
